 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Use the **`@needs_app_scope`** decorator, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app with `LaunchInfo.load_app()` and then pushes `app.app_context()`. The built-in `shell` and `routes` commands use it (`cli.py:999`, `cli.py:1059`).\n\n- **Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). Its `load_app()` method at line 333 finds and imports the app. The `TesselGroup` class (`cli.py:531`) calls it at lines 623 and 645 when it dispatches commands.\n- **Where to register commands:** `AppGroup` (`cli.py:405`) is the base of `TesselGroup`, and it wraps its commands with app scope automatically. Commands added with `@app.cli.command()` therefore get the app context without `@needs_app_scope`.\n\nI haven't tested this. It comes from reading `cli.py`, and I only grepped for the key definitions rather than reading the whole file.",
